  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Reduction of and Improved Operational Response to Gender-Based Violence through Camp Management and Site Planning Phase X</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2015, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) has been implementing a global project on reducing gender-based violence (GBV) through enhanced institutional risk mitigation efforts under the Safe from the Start Initiative supported by the United States Department of State Bureau of Population, Refugees and Migration. IOM&apos;s Global Safe from the Start project is now entering its tenth year of implementation. In Phase X, IOM continues to pursue key milestones set against commitments made by IOM under the 2021-2025 Roadmap of the Global Call to Action on Protection against GBV in Emergencies including: to strengthen risk mitigation and response capacities in key technical areas where IOM brings a strategic added-value to collective efforts on GBV - including Camp Coordination and Camp Management, Shelter and Settlements, Water, Sanitation and Hygiene, Displacement Tracking Matrix, and Health; to pursue the institutionalization and operationalization of the GBV in Crises Framework to foster more coherent and holistic responses of IOM to address GBV in crisis; and to continue supporting inter-agency initiatives from the Inter-Agency Standing Committee and United Nations-wide system on collective Protection against Sexual Exploitation and Abuse.</narrative>
  </description>
